# Shell scripts must always check out with LF endings. On Windows the default
# autocrlf converts them to CRLF, which breaks them under bash/WSL/Linux with
# `$'\r': command not found` (bit us on deploy.sh and would break the
# user-facing init-tidecloak.sh / bootstrap-tidecloak.sh on Linux/Mac).
*.sh text eol=lf

# The Tide login enclave integrity-checks tide_dpop_auth.html byte-for-byte. The
# canonical page is LF (9120 bytes); a Windows autocrlf checkout would rewrite it to
# CRLF, changing every byte, so an integrity check (and the gate's known-good sha256)
# fails. Pin it to LF everywhere so it can never ship platform-mangled.
tide_dpop_auth.html text eol=lf
